<title>EGYPT: EGYPTIAN FEB YR/YR INFLATION LOWER AT 5.4 PCT.</title>
<headline>EGYPTIAN FEB YR/YR INFLATION LOWER AT 5.4 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's consumer price index fell to 5.4 percent year-on-year in February, from 5.7 percent in January and 6.3 percent in February 1996, the government statistics office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The statistics showed the index for urban areas, set at a base of 100 in the financial year 1986/7, rose 0.2 percent in February 1997 to 376.6 from 375.7 in January 1997.</p>
<p>The index was 357.3 in February 1996.</p>
<p>					  Feb 1997  Jan 1997  Feb 1996</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		   +0.2	+0.4	+0.5</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		     +5.4	+5.7	+6.3</p>
<p>    INDEX  (base 1986/7)	  376.6     375.7     357.3</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/</p>
